x̂_s = M(x; c) with the listed blocks replaced by identity
if sigma in [σ_end, σ_start]: x̂ = x̂_cfg + w·(x̂_c − x̂_s)
if ρ≠0: f = std(x̂_c)/std(x̂), x̂ ← x̂·(ρ·f + 1−ρ)
Std is over the whole tensor.

σ_min<σ≤σ_max: x̂ = x̂_u + w(x̂_c−x̂_u)
else: x̂ = x̂_u (only uncond is run)
Post-CFG functions then run on the result.

pre_cfg: if σ outside [σ_end, σ_start] skip
if two outputs: cond ← op(cond − uncond) + uncond
else cond ← op(cond)

rotate: torch.rot90(x, k, dims=[3,2]), k∈{0,1,2,3}
flip: x-axis→flip dim2, y-axis→flip dim3
crop: x[:,:,y//8:y//8+h//8, x//8:x//8+w//8], offset clamped so at least 8 cells remain
